+## Classical determinant identities and block structure
+
+The determinant expectations \(A\) and \(B\) in Section 2 are zonoid and
+lift-zonoid volumes in the normalization \(Z(\nu)=\mathbb E[0,X]\) and
+\(\widehat Z(\nu)=\mathbb E[0,(1,X)]\). G. Koshevoy and K. Mosler,
+*Lift zonoids, random convex hulls and the variability of random vectors*,
+Bernoulli **4** (1998), 377–399, give the relevant determinant representation
+in Section 4, Theorem 4.1 and equation (4.3), printed p. 387 of the
+[primary author PDF](https://wisostat.uni-koeln.de/sites/dep_econometrics/pdf_publikationen/1998_KoshevoyM98.pdf).
+The determinant identity is background; the cone-law endpoint and stability
+assertions require the further arguments in entry005 and this supplement.
+
+The finite-support exact rank-two block structure has a matroid antecedent:
+J. van der Pol, Z. Walsh and M.C. Wigal, *Turán densities for matroid basis
+hypergraphs*, [arXiv:2502.03673v2](https://arxiv.org/html/2502.03673v2#S5),
+Section 5 and Lemma 5.2, printed pp. 14–15. They classify
+\(U_{3,4}\)-minor-free matroids as direct sums of matroids of rank at most two.
+Circuits of size at most three give that excluded-minor condition. Entry005 v4
+includes a direct proof for its almost-sure measure formulation; the present
+quantitative lemma estimates approximation from small expected cofactors.
 
