 ## Projection-body and recent mixed-volume comparisons
 
+The class \(\mathcal E_d\) is the familiar class of affine Cartesian products
+of centrally symmetric intervals and planar bodies, called Weil bodies in
+C. Saroglou, *On the shape of a convex body with respect to its second projection
+body*, [arXiv:1409.4347v2](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1409.4347v2), pp. 2–4.
+That paper relates the class to Weil's polytopal classification for homothety
+under the second projection-body operator and gives a three-dimensional zonoid
+endpoint with symmetric-cylinder equality (Theorem 1.2). These use a different
+functional from \(a(K)\); the common extremal class alone does not make their
+statements equivalent to entry005 v4's equality theorem or Theorem A here.
+The Weil reference listed there is W. Weil, *Über die Projektionenkörper
+konvexer Polytope*, Arch. Math. **22** (1971), 664–672. The original 1971
+article was not obtained, and no exact theorem number in it is asserted.
+
